 ## Overview
-A GPU-based brute-force method to convert a triangle mesh into a set of voxel points by dispatching one compute thread per grid cell and testing each cell's Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB) against all mesh triangles [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Geometry Shader Voxelization](2566-geometry-shader-voxelization.md) by using a compute shader with explicit AABB-triangle intersection tests rather than rasterization, and from [GPU Mesh Voxelization via Axis-Aligned Projection](2561-gpu-mesh-voxelization-via-axis-aligned-projection.md) by iterating all triangles per voxel rather than projecting triangles into grid slices.
